      "limitations": [
        "The source3.8packed-lime process consumes one kgof its lime market and one packing service. The market description says quicklime, but its actual dominant suppliers mill uncalcined crushed limestone; Quebec documentation explicitly excludes quicklime production. Native milled packed limestone is therefore the inventory-consistent counterpart. Reject both the old hydrated-lime candidate and a quicklime-name substitution: native quicklime includes kiln calcination and1.079kgdirectCO2at its in-pieces step, absent from the source grinding chain.",
        "Retain the source legacy name/CAS/product-description inconsistency as provenance, rather than pretending it was an unambiguous chemical declaration. Native complete packed limestone includes its own quarry, crushing, grinding, packing, heating and transport boundary. Source mine-co-product share, upstream sourcing, final delivery, packing, energy and internal uncertainty differ. Preserve kgwithout inventing CaCO3/CaO/Ca(OH)2stoichiometric, purity or yield factors.",
